{"id":"esercito","lemma":"esercito","pos":"adj","rank":704,"glosses":["exercised","practised","trained"],"ipa":"/eˈzɛr.t͡ʃi.to/","forms":{"feminine":"esercita","masculinePlural":"eserciti","femininePlural":"esercite"},"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2e/LL-Q652_%28ita%29-Crunchy_Cloaky_Crackdown-esercito.wav","examples":[{"text":"Mi esercito molte ore ogni giorno.","en":"I practice many hours every day.","words":[{"g":"me / myself"},null,{"g":"much, very much, a lot","l":"molto"},{"g":"now","l":"ora"},null,null],"phrases":[[4,6,"daily"]]},{"text":"Perché non si esercita più con me?","en":"Why doesn't he exercise with me anymore?","words":[{"g":"why / because"},{"g":"not"},{"g":"oneself"},null,{"g":"more"},{"g":"with"},{"g":"me"}]},{"text":"L'esercito era pieno di armi.","en":"The army had plenty of weapons.","words":[null,null,{"g":"to be","l":"essere"},{"g":"full"},{"g":"of"},{"g":"weapon, arms","l":"arma"}]},{"text":"Perché parla ancora dell'esercito?","en":"Why does he still talk about the army?","words":[{"g":"why / because"},{"g":"to talk, to speak","l":"parlare"},{"g":"still / again"},null,null]},{"text":"Il nuovo presidente vuole costruire l'esercito.","en":"The new president wants to build up the army.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"new"},{"g":"president"},{"g":"to want","l":"volere"},{"g":"to build, construct"},null,null]}]}